this year has been pretty weird for the  mac lineup because many of the macs we  were originally expecting to get haven't  showed up at all and are reportedly  being delayed with sources like ming chi  quo saying that we shouldn't expect the  mac pro the imac pro and even the mac  mini to get updated until next year and  out of nowhere apple gave us the max  studio which was almost a complete  surprise since we were expecting to get  the new high-end mac mini and that's  exactly what this video is going to be  about because we recently got some  bombshell leaks regarding proof that a  new mac mini has likely already been  created by apple and is waiting for  release but before i get into that major  leak i've got to go through all of the  previous pieces of evidence for why a  new mac mini should be coming soon first  of all the mac mini is now the only mac  for sale other than the mac pro that  still comes with an intel chip now  that's a problem because apple gave us a  two-year timeline for the transition to  their own apple silicon chips which  means that basically every intel mac  should be getting an apple silicon  replacement and according to mark german  who is by far the most reliable apple  analyst and leaker the two-year timeline  should be completed by apple's wwdc  keynote in june basically two years  after apple announced the transition now  that doesn't mean that the macs  necessarily have to be shipping by then  but they'll at least be announced by  june according to mark so what this  basically means is that apple either  needs to replace the intel mac mini with  a new apple silicon based model or they  can simply discontinue it just like they  did with the 27-inch imac and thankfully  we actually have some evidence for there  being a brand new mac mini out there  somewhere in the world right now but  let's go all the way back to the  beginning of the leaks for the new mac  mini to prove that we've been expecting  it for a while in the summer of last  year dylan dkt tweeted out that he was  expecting a new m1x mac mini to release  alongside the new macbook pros and even  before that john prosser released  renders of the leaked mac mini design  also mentioning that it could  potentially come as soon as the end of  the year but of course it got delayed  because apple wanted all of the  attention on the macbook pros instead on  top of that mark german has been  expecting a new mac mini ever since may  of last year with details pointing to it  coming with an m1 pro and m1 max chip  just like we got with the macbook pros  later that year he ended up mentioning  the high-end mac mini again in august  saying that it's coming in the next  several months and then in october right  after apple's macbook pro event he once  again confirmed that it should be coming  sometime in 2022.  he continued to mention it in december  and january reporting the apple is  likely to bring the m1 pro chip to  another mac in the first half of the  year which could be a higher end mac  mini or imac and then over the next  couple of months he made another three  reports concerning the mac mini even  going as far as to say that he's  expecting one high-end mac mini with an  m1 pro chip and one with an m2 chip  coming in the first half of 2022 but  then apple's march event came around and  while it seemed basically 100 likely  that apple was going to release a new m1  pro and m1 max high-end mac mini we of  course got the max studio instead which  was a huge surprise and since that  machine is basically a larger and more  expensive mac mini that starts with the  m1 max chip it could totally make sense  for apple to release a high-end mac mini  to replace the intel model but maybe  with just the m1 pro chip as the sole  option instead of the m1 max since  that's what the mac studio comes with  but moving on to the latest leaks that  came after the march event 95 mac had an  exclusive leak where they found internal  code referring to two new mac mini  models one being codenamed j473  which is the new m2 mac mini expected to  be announced sometime later this year  and then the j474  which is the m2 pro mac mini coming  later down the road possibly next year  and perhaps the most interesting part  was when 95 mac said that apple had  plans to introduce high-end versions of  the mac mini with the m1 pro and m1 max  chips but they were scrapped to make way  for the mac studio so what it makes it  seem like is that apple never even  planned to release the m1 pro mac mini  since they've been working on the mac  studio for a while which would mean that  we'd have to wait for the m2 mag mini to  come later this year but wait we've  actually got some new proof that the  high-end m1 pro and m1 max mac mini  actually does exist first of all if we  go back to may of 2021 when mark german  discussed a new more powerful mac mini  with the code name j374  the interesting part is that the new m2  and m2 pro mac minis that 95 mac leaked  have code names of j473  and j474 so j374 is still out there  somewhere and just in case you think  that the j374 mac mini turned out to be  the max studio the r evil quanta leak  found references to both j 374 and  j375 and 95 mac was able to confirm that  j375 is actually the code name for the  mac studio so with that said the j374  mac mini is still out there somewhere  and there's a chance that this could  actually be the high-end m1 pro mac mini  and finally with all of that out of the  way we just got a bombshell leak from  apple developer steve trouten smith he  was able to find a reference to a brand  new unreleased mac mini within the  studio displays firmware that it shipped  with titled the mac mini 10 comma 1  which means that apple could have been  originally planning to release the m1  pro mac mini alongside the studio  display but ended up releasing the max  studio instead now steve originally  guessed that it would be the m2 mac mini  but later the next day he revised his  guess and he now believes that the  unreleased mac mini is actually one that  comes with both the m1 pro and m1 max  chips and while it might seem weird to  have an m1 max option because that's the  chip the mac studio starts with steve  argues that it might be enough to push  people to bump up to the mac studio if  there's not a lot between them but i  personally think a model with just the  m1 pro chip makes sense because that'll  force you to pay more for the max studio  now with that said if steve is right and  we actually get an m1 pro mac mini later  this year this means that it could  technically be released at any time  since that ship has been around since  last year but wait the evidence gets  even better because way back in february  apple registered three new macs in the  eurasian database two desktop macs and  one laptop now one of those turned out  to be the mac studio and i personally  believe that the other registered  desktop mac model is the upcoming mac  mini and this leaves just one laptop  which i think has a chance to be the  redesigned macbook air because of some  recent major leaks and reports just days  ago mark grumman released his latest  power on newsletter where he mentioned  that apple is gearing up to launch some  new macs in the next few months and what  better place to do so than  wwdc specifically he said that there are  two new macs coming around the middle of  the year or early next year which  perfectly lines up with the two  unreleased macs that apple registered  with the eurasian database however for  the first time in months he completely  changed his predictions to say that one  of those is likely to be the new macbook  air with another model being potentially  an updated mac mini and the crazy thing  is that ming chaquel believes that the  2022 redesigned macbook air is coming as  soon as the end of the second quarter  which is in june with a new design more  color options and the m1 chip yes the  same m1 chip that we already have so if  this turns out to be true it would mean  that both the new m1 macbook air and the  m1 pro mac mini can technically be  released at any point because they're  using older chips that we already have  on other macs and this would mean that  apple can release these two macs in the  summertime just like mark german was  predicting and then they can wait until  the fall to release the new m2 chip  within the macbook pro and likely the  low end base m2 mac mini and this  actually makes sense because there have  been some reports pointing to the m2  chip arriving in the second half of 2022  including from the site commercial times  as well as mark german who believes the  m2 macbook pro will come by the end of  the year so with that said the m1 pro  mac mini and redesigned m1 macbook air  could end up coming sometime this summer  however  a couple of sources disagree with this  idea including 9 to 5 mac who believe  apple completely cancelled the m1 pro  mac mini in favor of simply releasing  the m2 mac mini this year and waiting  for the m2 pro version next year they  also believe that the redesigned macbook  air will in fact come with the m2 chip  instead of the m1 like ming chi quo  predicted and on top of that leek's  apple pro from eyedrop news believes  that apple is actually going to be  releasing two m2 macs at their wwdc  event with one of them for sure being a  mac mini and the other one potentially a  24 inch imac or a 13 inch base macbook  pro but either way whatever ends up  happening i think it's pretty clear that  we are in fact getting either an m1 pro  or m2 mac mini later this year  potentially as soon as wwdc in the  summer and i think that's some pretty  awesome news so hopefully you enjoyed  this video and if you did go ahead and  click the circle above to subscribe for  more videos like this one and be sure to  check out one of those two right over  there thanks for watching and we'll see  you in the next video  [Music]

